 result←object New arg;parent;name;∆style;props;newobj;∆border;t;stretch;extent
⍝ Note that for style∊0 2, any heights are ignored and all vertical sizing is determined solely by font size and row count.
⍝ For style∊1, size/extent determine total height (minimum 5 char-units, no maximum)
⍝ Maximum number of rows displayed (style≠1) keeps total default control height ≤22 char-units for whatever font is in use

 (parent name)←object ⍝ Separate non-standard two-part argument
 (∆style ∆border)←arg ##._supp.GetInitialProps'style' 'border'
 extent←_size⌈5 0×1∊∆style ⍝ style=1 has a different default size, override it
 stretch←59 0×~1∊∆style ⍝ Centering will need to happen as if it is sized for style=1, so adjust for default 'size'
 arg←(parent:parent ⋄ border:∆border ⋄ stretch:stretch ⋄ extent:extent)##.##.New.Center arg

⍝ We'll try always using a ComboEx and hope there are no incompatibilities that require old Combo.
 props←'ComboEx'('Visible' 0) ⍝ Define properties that must be used during creation
 props,←⊂'Border'∆border ⍝ Set border upon creation ⍝? It cannot be changed later
 props,←⊂'Style'('DropEdit' 'Simple' 'Drop'⊃⍨0 1 2⍳⊃1 2∩∆style) ⍝? Create-only style?
 props,←(~1∊∆style)/⊂'Rows' 4 ⍝ Set the default size for non-Simple types
 props,←⊂'HScroll'(¯2×~8∊∆style) ⍝? Create-only style
 props,←⊂'VScroll'(¯1×16∊∆style) ⍝? Create-only style
 ⍝? style=128 (hide scroll bar) is not available in Dyalog

 newobj←⎕VGET(parent⍕⍛,'.',name)##.##.∆WC props ⍝ Create the actual Dyalog object with required parameters
 newobj._style←+/∆style ⍝ Pre-set the _style so 'where' & friends can use it during initializatin
 result←parent newobj ##.##.New.Initialize arg ⍝ Complete standard class-initialization procedure
